   "subject": "filter.maf",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m attempting to filter my SNP dataset, which is a gl object, using the gl.filter.maf function.</div><div><br></div><div><div>/// GENLIGHT OBJECT /////////</div><div><br></div><div> // 43 genotypes,  40,764 binary SNPs, size: 5.7 Mb</div><div> 497318 (28.37 %) missing data</div><div><br></div><div> // Basic content</div><div>   @gen: list of 43 SNPbin</div><div><br></div><div> // Optional content</div><div>   @ind.names:  43 individual labels</div><div>   @loc.names:  40764 locus labels</div><div>   @chromosome: factor storing chromosomes of the SNPs</div><div>   @position: integer storing positions of the SNPs</div><div>   @pop: population of each individual (group size range: 5-19)</div><div>   @other: a list containing: elements without names </div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m getting the following error:</div><div><br></div><div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">Error in if (nLoc(x) != nrow(x@other$loc.metrics)) { : </font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\">  argument is of length zero</font></div></div><div><br></div><div>I also get this error when I try to do the gl.report.maf, but I don&#39;t have any trouble filtering using any of the other filtering functions. Can you please let me know what I may be doing wrong? Please let me know what other information you would need to answer my question. The files are too large to attach, but I can provide them with another means if necessary.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "aken7fs1AQAJ",
   "from": "Arthur Georges",
   "author": "a3ea45e87285d820",
   "date": "2019-07-10T23:15:42Z",
